  ('dcdf28f7-ed91-5638-9dcd-335fb025fe1d', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g12-informative-writing'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The writer considers moving paragraph 3 (sentences 9 to 11) so that it comes before paragraph 2. Which evaluation of this change is most accurate?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The change would help, because the report should end with the drilling, which is its most exciting part.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"excitement-over-logic"},{"text":"The change would make no difference, because each paragraph of an informative report stands completely on its own.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-cohesion"},{"text":"The change would weaken the report, because sentence 9 assumes readers already know that gases are measured, which paragraph 2 explains.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The change would help, because readers should learn about volcanic ash before they learn about drilling.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-dependency"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The change would weaken the report, because sentence 9 assumes readers already know that gases are measured, which paragraph 2 explains.$q$, $q$Sentence 9 depends on the gas measurements described in paragraph 2, so each idea builds on the one before it in the current order. Moving the dating paragraph first would make "a gas measurement" appear before readers know what is being measured.$q$, 'draft', '6914d92c-8813-5988-ae30-baed5619fd55')
