  ('98a0a121-8091-52db-93dd-a0852446228b', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g12-informative-writing'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Which statement best describes how paragraphs 2 through 4 are organized, and why that order is effective?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They compare two cities point by point, so readers can decide which city handles lighting better.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misidentifies-structure"},{"text":"They follow time order, tracing light pollution from its earliest appearance to the present, so readers see how it developed.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misidentifies-structure"},{"text":"They move from the forms of light pollution to its effects to a response, so readers understand the problem before learning how a town addressed it.","is_correct":true},{"text":"They present a solution first and the problem last, so readers end with the most serious information.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-order"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They move from the forms of light pollution to its effects to a response, so readers understand the problem before learning how a town addressed it.$q$, $q$Paragraph 2 classifies the forms, paragraph 3 explains effects on wildlife and paragraph 4 describes Pell Harbor's response, so each paragraph builds on the one before. The report gives no dates for the spread of light pollution, so it is not organized by time.$q$, 'draft', 'e7e3a0fd-c9e7-5cfa-ab5e-8d45f6968b80')
