  ('8bb4a6ac-aaff-56bf-8825-0fa6eba3345c', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g12-informative-writing'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The writer wants to add a sentence after sentence 3 that introduces the topic by previewing how the rest of the report is organized. Which sentence does this best?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Laying cables across oceans was first attempted long ago with telegraph wires.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-focus-history"},{"text":"Understanding how these cables are built, how their signals are boosted and how they are repaired reveals the physical network behind everyday online life.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The fibers inside a cable are made of extremely pure glass.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"The internet has changed the way people live in many ways.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-broad"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Understanding how these cables are built, how their signals are boosted and how they are repaired reveals the physical network behind everyday online life.$q$, $q$The correct sentence names the three topics of paragraphs 2, 3 and 4 in order and states why they matter. The sentence about pure glass is accurate but too narrow to preview the report.$q$, 'draft', 'cee10173-2559-5bbe-bef4-df294d6d2c8c')
