   $q$Which revision of sentence 7 gives the most precise information and fits sentences 5 and 6?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The rest of the clothes went to lots of other places.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"vague-wording"},{"text":"The remaining 35 percent, too worn or stained to wear, went to recyclers or, as a last resort, to a landfill.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The remaining 80 percent were thrown away as trash.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"miscalculates-share"},{"text":"Some of the clothes were probably given to friends.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The remaining 35 percent, too worn or stained to wear, went to recyclers or, as a last resort, to a landfill.$q$, $q$Since 20 percent and 45 percent account for 65 percent, the remaining share is 35 percent, and the correct revision also names where it went. The 80 percent choice ignores the 45 percent sold in bales in sentence 6.$q$, 'draft', '31909953-9797-570c-b63c-01fd6a2df270')
